;=============================================================================
; ExportClass.exp  -  the export list for ExportClass (the myExport template).
;
; YOU DO NOT NEED THIS FILE IN AN APPGEN APPLICATION. Add the myExportGlobal
; extension to every app in the suite and Clarion writes these same lines into
; the owning DLL's .EXP for you, from the class registry - see myExport.tpl.
;
; This copy is for a HAND-CODED multi-DLL build, where nothing generates an
; .EXP for you. Paste the lines below under the EXPORTS line of the .EXP of the
; DLL that compiles ExportClass.clw, and give each project its defines:
;
;   the DLL that owns the class   _myExportLinkMode_=>1  _myExportDllMode_=>0
;   every app that imports it     _myExportLinkMode_=>0  _myExportDllMode_=>1
;
; These are Clarion's mangled names, so they follow the class's prototypes: if
; you add, remove or re-prototype a method, regenerate this list or the link
; will fail. The reliable way to regenerate it is to let AppGen do it (generate
; any DLL app that has myExportGlobal on it and copy the EXPORTCLASS lines out
; of its .EXP); the names can also be read out of a compiled ExportClass.obj.
;
; Generated from Clarion 12.0.13941 AppGen output.  73 entries.
;=============================================================================
